INT. RIVERSIDE BANQUET HALL - WEDDING AFTERPARTY - NIGHT

Streamers. Half-eaten cake. A DJ booth abandoned mid-song. The last guests have gone. Two people remain.

Gwen, 30s, in a bridesmaid dress and one shoe, drags a folding chair into the middle of the floor and drops onto it like she's been shot.

GWEN
Best. Wedding. Ever.

The side door SLAMS open. Ash, 30s, they/them, enters in a velvet blazer, holding a tray of leftover champagne flutes like a waiter at a very strange restaurant.

ASH
You did not say that during the toast.

GWEN
During the toast I was holding in a sneeze and a sob.

ASH
(setting down the tray)
Same thing, honestly.

Gwen grabs a flute. Ash takes one. They clink. Neither drinks.

GWEN
Okay. Real talk. Did you see the groom's uncle?

ASH
The one who made the toast to "his many wives"?

GWEN
He has one wife.

ASH
Then he's very ambitious.

Gwen cracks up. Ash pretends not to be pleased.

GWEN
You're good at this, you know that? Making people feel like they're not at a funeral.

ASH
They are at a funeral. It's just a really good one.

The overhead speaker CRACKLES. A distant voice, faint and metallic, comes through the PA.

DJ (V.O.)
(over speaker)
Hey, uh, last song's still queued up. Should I play it?

GWEN
(to the ceiling)
What song?

DJ (V.O.)
It's, uh... it's labeled "DO NOT PLAY."

Gwen and Ash exchange a look.

ASH
Obviously play it.

GWEN
Ash, no.

ASH
Gwen. Yes.

The speakers hum. A single piano note. Another. Then a voice, a woman's voice, soft, singing in a language neither of them knows.

The room goes still. The streamers stop swaying. The candles on the tables light themselves, one by one, in a perfect ring around the dance floor.

GWEN
(whispering)
Please tell me that's the DJ's idea of a joke.

ASH
(not joking)
The DJ left at ten.

DJ (V.O.)
(over speaker, shaking)
Guys... I'm still in the booth. I didn't press anything.

The door at the end of the hall SWINGS open on its own. A figure in a long pale dress stands there, face hidden, hands folded in front like a bride.

GWEN
(small)
Is that... is that Priya's grandmother?

ASH
Priya's grandmother died in March.

GWEN
So that's a no.

The figure takes one step. The candles all lean toward it.

ASH
(very calm)
Okay. New plan.

GWEN
I love a new plan.

ASH
We run.

GWEN
Oh, I love that plan.

They bolt for the exit together. The side door SLAMS shut behind them. The song swells.

The figure lifts its veil.

Underneath, grinning, is the DJ.

DJ
(lowering the headset)
Gotcha.

DJ (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(over speaker, offended)
Hey! That's my line.
